y marks the start of the busiest stretch of the year for home sales. Many families want to buy and sell homes in the spring so they can move over the summer.Copyright ©2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. 87990cbe856818d5eddac44c7b1cdeb8Continue reading your article witha WSJ subscriptionSubscribe NowAlready a subscriber? Sign InFurther ReadingSlowing U.S. Home Construction Doesn’t Faze Japanese HomebuildersFannie Mae to Accept Crypto-Backed Mortgages for the First TimeVideosMost Popular NewsU.A.E. Wants to Force Hormuz Open and Is Willing to Join the FightThe Highs and Lows of My $939 Upgrade to United Business ClassAmerica Now Has an EV Rust Belt. High Gas Prices Won’t Rescue It.How a Massive KitKat Heist Turned Into Crisis PR GoldAnthropic Races to Contain Leak of Code Behind Claude AI AgentMost PopularOPINIONBirthright Citizenship Hits the Supreme CourtTrump Is Right on Birthright CitizenshipHormuz, ShmormuzTrump and the Hormuz StakesThe Tragic Tale of Tiger WoodsFurther ReadingSlowing U.S. Home Construction Doesn’t Faze Japanese HomebuildersFannie Mae to Accept Crypto-Backed Mortgages for the First Time",
